<%# locals: (label:, url:, variant: :secondary, size: :regular, full: true) %>
<%# One way in that leaves this site: the provider's start, a gem's sign-in
    method, or the owner path's "Sign in with %{provider} instead". A real
    button in a POST form with the form's token, sent without Turbo, since
    the answer is a whole page on another site (a provider's redirect) that
    Turbo's fetch could not follow. The provider's and a gem's are drawn
    alike: the card drew no gem's button, so it takes the provider's look. %>
<%= button_to label, url, method: :post, form: { data: { turbo: false } },
      class: [ Admin::Ui::ButtonComponent.classes(variant, size: size), ("w-full" if full) ].compact.join(" ") %>
